  "details": "Currently, an issue with modern audio is that very quiet sounds can be hard to hear at low volumes. However, turning up the volume can result in unintentional hearing damage as louder sounds exceed safe ranges as a result. This can be particularly difficult for those hard of hearing.\nBy adding an **Output Volume Limit**, also known as a \"Limiter\", a form of compression technique, loud sounds may be \"clamped\" to a specified volume.\n# Details\n- An \"Audio Volume Limit\" slider will be provided, similar to the upcoming Noise Gate slider\n- At 100%, audio will be clamped to +/-0db, if enabled.\n- At 0%, audio will be clamped to the minimum audible range (usually -60db)\n- Audio *above* the set range **will be clamped** via a compressor, \"flattening\" loud sounds\n- Audio *below* the range will be unaffected\n- Audio limitations will be applied application-wide, at the end of audio processing before output to user speakers or audio monitoring equipment\n- This will result in a loss of \"peak\" volume in exchange for louder overall volumes and safer listening limits.\nE.G. If the AVL is set to -10db, audio above -10db will be clamped to -10db. **Audio below the limit will be unaffected** and maintain intended volume.\n# Related Feedback\n[Built-in audio volume limiter](https://feedback.vrchat.com/feature-requests/p/built-in-audio-volume-limiter)",
